%S A402345 1,5,121,28561,71385601,1872712598261,510925709066955625,
%T A402345 1443134633691436850272225,42112012462508110293785705054209,
%U A402345 12682456809311721350817701357733298515749,39396218792467346390886562920071491558570190350809,1261873790121868616542665698426881104409710581607819451705969
%N A402345 Number of domino tilings of a 2n X 2n cylindrical grid.
%C A402345 For n >= 2, a(n) is the number of perfect matchings of the Cartesian product P_2n X C_2n. For n = 1 the cycle C_2 has two edges between its two vertices, and each of them counts as a separate domino, as in A335586.
%C A402345 a(n) is the term k = 2n of the sequence for C_2n X P_k: A006253 for n = 2, A028477 for n = 3, A028479 for n = 4.
%C A402345 The formula comes from Kasteleyn's method: the cylinder is planar, and the edges that cross the seam take the opposite sign.
%C A402345 a(n) is a square for even n (see the formula for a(2*m)). For odd n <= 45 the only square is a(3) = 13^4.
%H A402345 Dawid Ryłko, <a href="/A402345/b402345.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..44</a>
%H A402345 Dawid Ryłko, <a href="https://dawidrylko.github.io/lattice-dimers/notes/dominoes/cylinders.html">Dominoes: tilings of cylinders</a>.
%H A402345 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/PerfectMatching.html">Perfect Matching</a>.
%F A402345 a(n) = Product_{j=1..n} Product_{k=1..n} (4*cos(j*Pi/(2*n+1))^2 + 4*sin((2*k-1)*Pi/(2*n))^2).
%F A402345 a(n) = Resultant(P(x), Q(x)), where P(x^2) = U(2*n, x/2) and Q(x) = 2*T(n, (x+2)/2) + 2, with T and U the Chebyshev polynomials of the first and second kind.
%F A402345 a(2*m) = Resultant(P(x), 2*T(m, (x+2)/2))^2, with P as above for n = 2*m.
%F A402345 lim_{n->oo} log(a(n))/(4*n^2) = A143233.
%F A402345 a(n) ~ 2^(1/8) * (sqrt(2) - 1)^(n - 1/2) * exp(2*G*n*(2*n+1)/Pi), where G is the Catalan constant A006752. - _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Nov 17 2026
%e A402345 a(1) = 5: on the 2 X 2 cylinder each cell is joined to its row neighbor by 2 edges and to its column neighbor by 1 edge, so a(1) = 2*2 + 1*1 = 5.
%t A402345 Table[Resultant[ChebyshevU[2*n, Sqrt[x]/2], 2*ChebyshevT[n, x/2 + 1] + 2, x], {n, 0, 12}] (* _Vaclav Kotesovec_, Nov 17 2026 *)
%o A402345 (PARI) a(n) = my(P = substpol(polchebyshev(2*n, 2, x/2), x^2, x)); polresultant(P, subst(2*polchebyshev(n, 1, x/2) + 2, x, x + 2));
%Y A402345 Cf. A004003 (2n X 2n square), A335586 (2n X 2n torus), A402163, A143233.
%Y A402345 Number of perfect matchings of the graph C_2m X P_n: A006253 (m=2), A028477 (m=3), A028479 (m=4), A028481 (m=5), A028483 (m=6), A028485 (m=7), A028487 (m=8).
%K A402345 nonn,new
%O A402345 0,2
%A A402345 _Dawid Ryłko_, Nov 17 2026
